 "key_big": "i² = −1.",
 "key_sub": "Combine real parts with real parts and imaginary parts with imaginary parts.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li><i>i</i> = √(−1), so <i>i</i><sup>2</sup> = −1. Powers of <i>i</i> repeat every 4: <i>i</i>, −1, −<i>i</i>, 1.</li><li>A complex number is <i>a</i> + <i>bi</i>: real part <i>a</i>, imaginary part <i>b</i>.</li><li>Add or subtract real parts with real parts and imaginary parts with imaginary parts.</li><li>Multiply like binomials, then replace <i>i</i><sup>2</sup> with −1. (<i>a</i> + <i>bi</i>)(<i>a</i> − <i>bi</i>) = <i>a</i><sup>2</sup> + <i>b</i><sup>2</sup>.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(3 + 2<i>i</i>)(1 − 4<i>i</i>)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3 − 12<i>i</i> + 2<i>i</i> − 8<i>i</i><sup>2</sup></p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3 − 10<i>i</i> + 8</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 11 − 10<i>i</i></p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Using <i>i</i><sup>2</sup> = 1</td><td><i>i</i><sup>2</sup> = −1.</td></tr><tr><td>Subtracting only the real parts</td><td>Subtract both parts.</td></tr><tr><td>Squaring each part separately</td><td>(<i>a</i> + <i>bi</i>)<sup>2</sup> has a middle term 2<i>abi</i>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does TEKS 2A.7A ask?",
   "a": "Add, subtract, and multiply complex numbers."
  },
  {
   "q": "Is every real number a complex number?",
   "a": "Yes. 5 = 5 + 0i."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is a conjugate?",
   "a": "a − bi is the conjugate of a + bi; their product is a real number."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why do complex numbers matter?",
   "a": "They give solutions to equations like x² + 4 = 0."
  }
